      "text": "We start with the given equation:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right) = 12\n\\]\n\nLet \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). Then the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\ny^2 + y = 12\n\\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation which can be rewritten as:\n\n\\[\ny^2 + y - 12 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 1 \\), and \\( c = -12 \\). Plugging in these values, we get:\n\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-12)}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 48}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 7}{2}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions for \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 + 7}{2} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = \\frac{-1 - 7}{2} = \\frac{-8}{2} = -4\n\\]\n\nSo, we have two cases to consider:\n\n1. \\( y = 3 \\)\n2. \\( y = -4 \\)\n\nFirst, consider \\( y = 3 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 16 = 3(3x - 4)\n\\]\n\\[\n4x - 16 = 9x - 12\n\\]\n\\[\n-16 + 12 = 9x - 4x\n\\]\n\\[\n-4 = 5x\n\\]\n\\[\nx = -\\frac{4}{5}\n\\]\n\nNext, consider \\( y = -4 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 16 = -4(3x - 4)\n\\]\n\\[\n4x - 16 = -12x + 16\n\\]\n\\[\n4x + 12x = 16 + 16\n\\]\n\\[\n16x = 32\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 2\n\\]\n\nThe possible values for \\( x \\) are \\( x = -\\frac{4}{5} \\) and \\( x = 2 \\). The greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
